---
// Mounted once (BaseLayout): animates every <details> element's open/close
// site-wide (Tools, Glossary, Certifications, ATT&CK/D3FEND maps, the Cheat
// Sheets, the Event ID / Network Ports / HTTP Status / OSI reference pages,
// and the artifact-parser tools that render a <details> results block)
// instead of the native instant toggle. See src/scripts/animatedDetails.ts
// for the behaviour and its guardrails (reduced-motion no-op, doesn't
// intercept programmatic opens).
//
// PAY-FOR-WHAT-YOU-USE: BaseLayout wraps ~1,700 prerendered pages, but only
// ~20 of them contain a <details> element at all — the overwhelming majority
// are generated detail pages (glossary terms, ATT&CK/D3FEND techniques, event
// IDs, blog/lab posts) with nothing collapsible on them. So the mount below is
// a tiny gate: it checks for a single <details> in the document and only then
// dynamically imports the animation module. Vite code-splits a dynamic import
// into its own chunk, so the animation code is never fetched, parsed, or
// executed on a page that has no <details> — only the few bytes of the gate
// itself ship everywhere.
//
// The gate is a runtime DOM query on purpose rather than a per-page opt-in
// prop: it is self-maintaining (a page that later grows a <details>, or a
// shared component like RecycleBinParser/LnkParser/EmailHeaderAnalyzer/
// DeobfuscatorBuilder that renders one, is covered automatically) and it
// cannot drift out of sync with the markup the way a hand-maintained page
// list would.
//
// Reduced motion is checked here too, ahead of the import — animateDetails()
// already no-ops under it, but bailing first means reduced-motion visitors
// never fetch the chunk at all. (Invariant 12: the native instant toggle is
// itself a fully visible, settled state, so skipping this entirely is the
// correct reduced-motion behaviour, not a degradation.) With JS disabled the
// <details> elements are plain, fully-working native disclosure widgets.
---

<script>
  // @ts-nocheck — vanilla DOM client script
  function init() {
    if (!document.querySelector('details')) return;
    if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;
    import('../scripts/animatedDetails').then(function (m) {
      Array.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll('details'), m.animateDetails);
    });
  }
  if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', init);
  else init();
</script>
